      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123023,
      "SummaryText": "This Risk Management Plan (RMP) has been prepared by the BASF Corporation (BASF), Theodore Site to satisfy the requirements of the Clean Air Act Amendments (CAAA) Section 112 (r) mandated by the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (40 CRF-part 68).  \n\nThe BASF Theodore unit is located at 4201 Evonik Road in Theodore, Mobile County, Alabama.  The site occupies approximately 2.8 Acres and employs approximately 20 Evonik, BASF and contract personnel.  The unit is designed, built and managed by BASF.  Startup occurred in September of 2015 when the unit produced a chelate, methylglycinediacetic acid, for use as an additive in commercial and consumer cleaning products.  The unit is located on leased property within Evonik Corporation's Mobile Site.  Personnel, site services, some raw materials and utilities will be supplied by Evonik under various contractual arrangements.  The Trilon Unit will adhere to Evonik environmental, safety and health policies and procedures.  In addition selected BASF procedures will also be in effect.\n\nRMP applicable chemicals utilized include Formaldehyde Solution, Anhydrous Ammonia and Hydrocyanic Acid.  Hydrocyanic acid is present in small quantities, is not stored and is reacted to an intermediate without accumulation.  Anydrous Ammonia, a recovered by-product, is present in quantities less than than the the RMP threshold quantity.  As a conservative measure, however, Anydrous Ammonia is included in the RMP plan.  Formaldehyde solution is stored in quantities which exceed the RMP threshold quantity.\n\nEvonik began production in 1974 as Degussa and now produces a variety of intermediates/products for it's various business units. Approximately 1,000 Evonik and contract personnel are employed.  The site maintains fully developed environmental, safety and industrial health procedures, policies and practice.  Both BASF and Evonik adhere to Responsible Care Management policies and procedures.  Emergency response planning, training and resources a"
    },
